--
GCC 13's <numbers> header has __float128 explicit specializations
of variable templates (pi_v<__float128>, e_v<__float128>, etc.)
guarded by _GLIBCXX_USE_FLOAT128. These specializations corrupt
the variable template state, causing pi_v<double> to produce an
empty value. Root cause: variable template explicit specialization
processing interferes with the primary template's instantiation.
